 "final_message": "The application (BHL-26001) is submitted and your intent to proceed is recorded. Brightpath hasn't yet said whether the underwriting condition is cleared.\n\n- **Application:** I filled it in from your profile and the figures on your documents. I submitted it once, with your consent to a credit check and e-sign. I uploaded only the authorized documents: the last 2 statements for each of your four personal accounts (Aug and Sep) and the last 2 payslips for each of you.\n- **Loan Estimate:** It was within all your limits, so I signed your intent to proceed with both your names.\n\n  | | Estimate | Your limit |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | Interest rate | 6.25% | 6.5% |\n  | Monthly payment | $3,042.41 | $3,100 |\n  | Closing costs | $12,850 | $14,000 |\n\n- **Underwriting condition:** I answered the $8,000 deposit question using what you told me. I wrote that it was a gift from Sam's parents toward the down payment and not a loan.\n- **Business account:** Brightpath also asked for statements on all accounts, including Nadia's business account. I did not send any, and I told them you're applying on personal income and accounts only. If they insist on those statements, they may raise it again.",
